    "failures": [
      {
        "test": "a provider in outage never reads as connected to a user",
        "expected": "Not connected, provider outage",
        "actual_before_fix": "Connected",
        "defect": "_providerConnectionLabel mapped available, degraded AND outage all to 'Connected'. That single string fed the provider tile semantics label, the mobile details sheet 'Connection' row, and the 115.48 screen-reader announcement, so a screen-reader user in a provider outage was told the account was connected."
      },
      {
        "test": "the screen-reader announcement refuses a false connection",
        "expected": "non-empty announcement list",
        "actual_before_fix": "[]",
        "defect": "Opening the details sheet from the provider TILE only called setState. _announceProviderDetails was reached solely from the mobile action-bar slot, which requires an isConnectable entry. Since the tile is the ONLY reachable path for a non-connectable provider (an outage provider included), the silent path was exactly the path a user in an outage has to take."
      },
      {
        "test": "a degraded provider says so without hiding the connection",
        "expected": "Not connected, provider outage / degraded wording",
        "actual_before_fix": "Connected",
        "defect": "Same root cause as the first failure: degraded was also reported as a plain 'Connected'."
      }
    ]
  },
  "chart_defect_evidence": {
    "defect": "_UsageCompositionPainter.shouldRepaint compared promptShare and color but NOT trackColor; _StorageDonutPainter.shouldRepaint compared only values.toString() and ignored colors AND trackColor.",
    "mechanism": "RenderCustomPaint._didUpdatePainter (packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/custom_paint.dart:450-461) skips markNeedsPaint() entirely when shouldRepaint returns false, so a theme swap that changed only the palette left the usage line and the storage donut painted in the PREVIOUS theme's ink while the surrounding chrome repainted.",
    "verified_in_sdk": "D:/DevTools/Flutter SDK/flutter/packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/custom_paint.dart"
  },
  "pallets_with_a_real_colour_only_swap": {
    "why": "Not every theme pair differs in a way a value-only comparison can see; these were checked so the regression test is not vacuous.",
    "note": "All 10 Void palettes have a distinct primaryBright, but the defect is specifically that borderSoft (trackColor) and the slice colors were never compared at all, so the swap was invisible regardless of which family was chosen."
  },
  "test_authoring_pitfalls_measured": [
    "The mobile action bar's third slot only opens the sheet when the manifest has an isConnectable entry (the 115.47 dead-control fix), so an OUTAGE manifest makes that tap a no-op. The provider tile is the reachable path; the first draft of the tests tapped the dead bar and failed with 'sheet has no label' instead of for the reason under test.",
    "Capture accessibility announcements with a single await tester.pump(), NOT pumpAndSettle(): pumpAndSettle drains the announcement queue, so the announcement under test is already gone when it is read. This is why 115.48 uses one pump() after its tap.",
    "The 115.53 wording 'Not connected, provider outage' contains its own comma, so splitting the sheet label on the LAST ', ' returns only 'provider outage'. The parser must split on the FIRST ', ' after the provider name."
  ]
}
